sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v2-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Reproducibility package: 85/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "requirements.lock.txt pins the exact environment (Python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.10.7, pillow 12.0.0) and the venv matches it; the computation is fully deterministic with no RNG, so seeds are not needed; the self-test runs in about 3 s, writes to a temp directory, verifies the SHA pins and parity, and the CLI flags are documented via argparse and the README section; I re-ran the self-test and all checks pass. Deductions: the GIF subtitle hard-codes \"oblique V1 stripes (60 degrees)\" for a preset rendered at 45 degrees, so the shipped artefact mislabels its own parameters (-5); the README section quotes a parity bound of 6.7e-16 while the code reports 2.2e-16, a small environment-dependent inconsistency between documentation and output (-3); the default PNG/CSV/GIF outputs are written into the repository root and docs/media with no output manifest or artifact hash, so a re-run silently overwrites the audited artefacts (-4); the docstring does not list the CLI flags, which are only discoverable via --help (-3). Evidence: requirements.lock.txt L1–L25: Exact pins incl. matplotlib==3.10.7, numpy==2.5.4, pillow==12.0.0; matches ./venv <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/requirements.lock.txt#L1-L25>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1628–L1716: Deterministic self-test: SHA pins, parity, map round-trip, negative control, FFT checks; writes only to tempdir <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1628-L1716>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1559–L1564: GIF label '(60 deg)' for fig33_rhombic_even_roll whose pattern_angle_deg is 45 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1559-L1564>; README.md L484–L495: Author's description: outputs, --gif flag, and the 6.7e-16 parity figure <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/README.md#L484-L495>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.85"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Reproducibility package' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" .
}

